WEBVTT

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.630
2045.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.180
World War III breaks out.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.430
"Tactical Dolls Mechanical life forms
visually indistinguishable from humans."
Tactical Dolls,
indistinguishable from humans,

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.270
"Tactical Dolls Mechanical life forms
visually indistinguishable from humans."
are deployed by military
organizations all around the world.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.570
And after the war ends,

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.950
the T-Dolls of the major military
manufacturer, Sangvis Ferri,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.620
"Sangvis Ferri A major military
manufacturing company that
rebelled against humanity."
suddenly rebel against humanity.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.370
"Sangvis Ferri A major military
manufacturing company that
rebelled against humanity."
The private military company, Griffin,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.830
"Griffin A private military company."

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:40.950
"Griffin A private military company."
sends its elite AR Team to find the cause
of the rebellion and put a stop to it.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.870
"AR Team Griffin's elite T-Doll unit."
sends its elite AR Team to find the cause
of the rebellion and put a stop to it.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.580
Sangvis reinforcements incoming!

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.000
Estimated arrival time, 15 seconds!

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.500
There are too many!

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.550
Try to save ammo!

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.930
It's all they can do to
take care of themselves!

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.590
They don't have the strength to...

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.470
I've come to deliver death.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:11.440
"S09 Area, Carpathian Mountains"

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.630
Griffin T-Dolls?

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.100
What are they doing out here?

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:45.810
Griffin did a mission here to
wipe out any Sangvis in the area.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.020
They were probably separated
from the main unit,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.730
and then abandoned at some point.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:53.230
Abandoned...

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:54.730
What's the plan, M4?

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.030
Take them with us?

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.200
Um...

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.410
Impossible. They're not
capable of moving silently.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.450
We are.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.000
Don't worry.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.870
If they're in offline mode,
the Sangvis won't notice them.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:10.380
We'll continue our mission
and leave them alone.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.380
O-Okay...

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:26.850
Confirming coordinates. V6J69-HJYRV.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:30.310
Clear weather. No wind. Clear visibility.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.860
Persica, this is AR Team.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.230
Heyo.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.240
Reporting in.
At the Sangvis recon base HQ,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.870
we found a career file labeled "Lyco,"
as well as the location of research data.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.370
Me! I found it!

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.790
Great. And?

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:52.790
The data from when "Lyco" was alive is
located in a mainframe in Safehouse 3.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:56.880
We will now head there, recover it,
and send it to 16LAB.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.260
Okay. Great.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.810
Let's hurry!
The Sangvis are waiting for us!

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:06.970
Get a hold of yourself.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.020
We're not here to have fun.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.770
Let's go, Captain.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.940
AR Team, begin the mission!

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:01.500
Hey, what do you think our
objective is for this mission?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.970
What are you trying to say, AR15?

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:09.720
Persica originally gave us a mission
to recover experiment data.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.060
And now here we are in Sangvis territory,

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.640
looking for documents left by the dead.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:21.570
We're T-Dolls. We just
need to follow our mission.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.110
True.

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.240
I was just a little curious.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.290
We've reached the target point.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.040
Wow. Find the data?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.710
The OS is too old for us
to hack the login system.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.170
We'll need a password to boot it up.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:51.810
Um... 90WISHROCK.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.310
Then an X.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.350
All caps.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:58.850
Password accepted.
I'm looking through the database.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.940
Got it.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:03.780
Copy everything in the database
to your memory and bring it home.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.650
We're not sending it via wireless?

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:10.160
Nope. There's a chance
the Sangvis will take it.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.990
We can't let them have it.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.910
Blow the mainframe before you leave.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.370
Roger.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:22.090
So we're in Sangvis territory,
hacking a Sangvis database,

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.800
to get data the Sangvis
don't even know they have?

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:27.720
Like a treasure hunt!

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.470
Yes. And we're very grateful.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.220
You found quite a treasure for us.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.640
Somebody's broken into the comms line!

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.940
I am Agent, of the Sangvis Ferri.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:42.360
I've been awaiting your arrival.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.520
A High-End Model?

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.110
High-End...

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:50.110
There's something in here that
our master desires for their own.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:54.780
Unfortunately, the system
was too old for us to decipher.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:58.290
So you used us to get it?

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:02.630
Now our master will have the "answer"!

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:07.210
Once I've ripped you apart
and taken out your memory...

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.760
Sangvis detected!

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.300
They're close!

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.140
Party time!

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.220
We have to hang in there until
the copy operation's complete!

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.640
Prepare for combat!

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:20.140
Everyone, get ready to
intercept the enemy!

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.770
There are too many of them!

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.150
Try to save ammo!

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:24.770
That goes double for you, SOPII!

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:26.070
I know that!

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.570
AR15, watch my back.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:30.570
Leave it to me.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:34.030
Big Sis M16, help me track
the enemy's movements!

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:35.530
Sure thing.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:37.740
Everybody, just hang
in there a little more.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.450
When this is over,
we'll all go home together.

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:41.330
Right!

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:42.710
Open fire!

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.780
Heading 076, Distance 300!

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.780
Jaeger!

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.990
They just keep coming...

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:16.240
Can't we contact Persica?

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.120
The module automatically
cut the transmission

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:20.910
to keep any information
on the lab from leaking.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.670
There's still half the
data transmission left.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.080
Can you hang in there?

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.000
There's just not enough of us.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.750
If they launch another
attack of the same size...

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.050
There's a better way.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:36.510
If we can contact the ones
in the Support Units,

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:38.140
they'll help us.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.600
It's all they can do to
protect themselves!

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:42.180
They don't have the strength to...

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:45.900
No, they're waiting for their next order.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:50.820
M4, can you change our signal
to get them to back us up?

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:51.740
Roger.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:55.860
But someone will need to bring them here.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:09:00.040
AR15, SOPII! When you get close,
launch a forcible access attempt!

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.040
I'll rewrite your privileges!

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.410
Roger!

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.510
Hang in there till we get back!

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.380
It'll be just the two of us for a while.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.430
This'll be rough, but let's
make it through somehow.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:20.600
I'm sorry.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:23.850
I couldn't make the call when it counted.

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:26.440
I'm always relying on you for help.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.310
You're doing a good job.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:31.360
You haven't screwed anything up yet.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.690
Don't worry about it.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.370
There are more Jaegers?!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.040
I'm within range of the
unit's local area network.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.790
Forced access complete.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.930
Privilege rewrite complete.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:03.390
Changing command priority.
Changing mission type.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:09.900
Transfer complete!

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.320
Those Support Units
helped a lot, it looks like.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:15.030
Yeah. Let's get out of here.

00:10:15.030 --> 00:10:16.820
I won't let you escape.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:23.830
Big Sis M16, where are you?

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.620
You should be more concerned
about yourself, M4A1.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:34.750
I've come to deliver death.

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:37.550
Agent...

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.090
Fascinating...

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:43.100
Even your eyes just before
your death aren't like theirs.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:48.890
Did you think you could escape

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.230
after stealing something
so important to our master?

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.780
Stop talking, and go to hell!

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:58.030
You...

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:06.700
Big Sis M16! Are you okay?

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.410
I saved you again.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:09.910
You owe me one.

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.460
Are the others okay, you think?

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:15.670
We're back!

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.050
Sangvis reinforcements are en route.

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:21.760
We need to get out of here now.

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:24.550
Right.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.810
Command System activated.

00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:29.230
Satellite link activated.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:30.770
Loading battlefield module.

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:32.900
Loading area synchronization module.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.980
Deploying tactical map!

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:37.320
This is AR Team.
Do you read?

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:37.900
"T-Doll"

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.320
"T-Doll"
Loud and clear.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.320
"T-Doll Skorpion"
Just fine!

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:41.610
"T-Doll"

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.320
"T-Doll"
Communications are working fine!

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:47.450
I'm sorry. Please, take over for us.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:48.910
Don't worry, comrade!

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:52.040
This is our job!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.290
They don't even know they were abandoned.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.210
I'll withdraw as soon as possible.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:01.800
AR Team, can you get a clear look at
the battlefield from your location?

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.050
Yes.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.930
The third data house is
surrounded by Sangvis.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:09.060
We'll need to break through to retreat.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.390
All Griffins function as a mainframe,

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:14.810
giving orders to the
dummies via the network.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:18.610
But the Sangvis have a forward
command post that sends

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:20.940
all the signals that give orders.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.030
If you can bring down that command post,

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:26.910
you can neutralize the vast majority
of the enemy in the area.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:29.910
Most of the Sangvis
are patrolling this area.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.290
By destroying and occupying that location,

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:36.330
we can neutralize the enemy
and withdraw from the area.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:41.510
G43, please head to coordinates
X9CEM and defend the rear.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:42.510
Roger.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:44.930
Vz. 61, PPSh-41,

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:51.270
head to coordinates YK78Q and VL43B,
respectively, and defend our flanks.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:52.810
Roger!

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:54.230
Understood!

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:58.270
Sangvis reinforcements are on the move!

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:01.570
We're fine! Just go!

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.150
O-Okay!

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:06.530
Let's hurry.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.910
Those Support Units won't last long.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:11.160
Right.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.480
There! To the rear!

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:38.310
Incoming Sangvis Reinforcements!
Estimated arrival time, 15 seconds!

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:39.440
Roger.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:42.480
Last time the Sangvis failed when they
attacked from the base of the mountain.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:45.240
They may try to drop down on us!

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:48.870
G43, watch above you!

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.080
Roger!

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.620
You were right!

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:56.920
One hundred fifty meters away.
Adjusting RPG flight path... firing!

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:03.800
100% accuracy. 17 Sangvis shut down.

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:05.760
Three escaped!

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:07.470
Continuing fire!

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:12.310
The first wave of enemies was wiped out.

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:13.810
All your calls were accurate.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:16.730
Thank you for your orders, M4! <i>Danke!</i>

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:18.190
Next they'll come from both flanks!

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.650
Be careful!

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:20.940
Roger.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.230
Enemies sighted.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:28.360
We'll handle them all!

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.540
Okay!

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.160
It's safe here now!

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:38.710
How about your area, Skorpion?

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.330
All done.

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:42.540
That was a close one.

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:45.300
We've safely made it
through the first wave.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:48.220
AR Team, what about you?

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.510
We've reached the target point.

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:54.350
The Sangvis should have
a temporary HQ here.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:57.810
Three, two, one! Blow it!

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.730
--Clear!
--Clear!

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.610
Huh? It's empty?

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.080
A powerful Sangvis signal
is approaching this area!

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.540
Wait, more than one.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:20.460
Two... three...

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.550
Support units, be careful!

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:26.760
It's a trap!

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:38.100
It's over, little Griffin girls.

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:42.060
There's nothing left for you to do
but make a mess on the floor.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:45.400
AR Team will escape... I know it!

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:46.690
It's useless.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:50.990
All you're doing is buying time.

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:55.620
And we have all the time
in the world right now.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:00.330
I'm surprised.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.080
Even an old-generation T-Doll
destined for the scrap heap

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.340
can still run pretty fast.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:12.970
Come in! Come in!

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.140
Griffin Support Units!

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:15.800
What is your situations?

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.640
Get out of here.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.730
Find... commander...

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.850
Griffin Team, what's going on?

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:24.850
You can still move, huh?

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:27.440
But now it's over.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.280
I-It's over...

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:33.030
...for you!

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:38.370
Signal lost.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:40.500
Don't tell me they...

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.330
Damn it!

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.500
There's no time to waste.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.920
They left us a chance.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.000
We need to get out of here
as soon as possible.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.260
You're already relaxing?

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:55.300
Isn't that a little too soon?

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:58.430
It's that Sangvis from before!

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:01.640
Hide!

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:14.240
Big Sis M16, aim some
suppressing fire at the right Sangvis!

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:17.950
SOPII, AR15, let's work together
to take out the one on the left!

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.160
Roger!

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:23.410
Big Sis M16, now!

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:24.620
Right!

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.380
Where's the one on the right?

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.630
The window?

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:36.260
I need backup! M16 is pinned down!

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:42.890
Do you really have time to
worry about someone else?

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:49.940
Damn it! They're persistent!

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:54.860
We're leaving!

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:59.240
What's going on?

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:02.450
Are they predicting our movements somehow?

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:06.410
Yeah. They must be hacking
our Zener Protocol.

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.960
They'll know what our plans
are as soon as we do.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:12.130
Then how'd M16 beat that one back there?

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:16.010
Oh, first they beat me so bad
I could only move my left hand.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:20.180
Next, I got blown off my feet and luckily
landed right at point-blank range.

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:22.760
So much for that.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:27.690
Everyone, do you remember
our 7th Combat Module?

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:30.440
Yeah, of course.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:33.400
Let's let them peek all they like.

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:39.860
Their link signal disappeared.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.620
Your tricks won't save you.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:55.460
Huh?

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:57.090
So they found our weakness.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:59.880
Our superior firepower to our front

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:02.050
also means we're weak
to attacks from the side.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:03.510
And when we're firing,

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.100
we become essentially immobile
due to the need to resist the recoil,

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:07.810
limiting how much we can move.

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:09.140
But with two of us here,

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:11.900
we can cover the vast majority
of each other's blind spots.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.860
This distance... That weak weapon...

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:20.200
You can't even scratch us!

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.580
Now come out,
and we'll put an end to this!

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:24.870
Three versus two.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:26.620
Their numbers advantage is meaningless.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:29.160
I can handle this easily.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:31.120
Three directions...?

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:32.330
Three?

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:37.760
Where's the other one?

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:43.890
Know your place, fool!

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:47.470
That rusty old weapon can't
hurt us from that distance!

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:50.770
All right, then...

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.560
How about this, then?

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:56.230
Eat this, Sangvis monsters!

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:09.450
So the attacks from the sides were decoys?

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.670
To keep me from looking up...

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:19.340
This thing won't do any good
if you're too close, after all.

00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:21.130
A 40mm grenade.

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.340
You Griffin trash...

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:25.550
Begone!

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.100
High End...

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:35.770
The end.

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.570
"Luckily landed right
at point-blank range."

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:40.030
Well done.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:41.820
You underestimated us.

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:44.740
We've worked together on
many operations just like this,

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:47.450
even without our Zener Protocol.

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:50.250
I guess we're about done, then.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:53.000
But the Support Units...

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:55.960
M4, don't forget.

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:59.210
Both they, and we,
were simply following orders.

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:00.840
Understood.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:03.090
I'll bring back the data no matter what.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.180
No matter what.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.640
So, now what?

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:11.600
They massively outnumbered us.

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:14.190
If they surround us, we're finished.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:18.060
We'll use backup plan C.

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:19.610
Just like we discussed.

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:24.110
So I'm supposed to go to
Griffin HQ and get backup? Myself?

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:28.620
Yeah. We'll split up and draw the
enemy's attention. Buy you time.

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.620
But there are Agents here!

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:34.080
And if the Sangvis
catch you, you'll all...

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:38.130
Get going.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:40.210
This is the best way.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:41.710
That's right.

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:46.680
You're the only one who can save us now.

00:21:54.060 --> 00:21:58.020
Okay. I promise, I'll find a
commander we can trust.

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:18.790
I promise, I'll find a
commander we can trust.

00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:29.510
Gentiane.

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:30.800
Gentiane!

00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:48.200
Thanks... yeah.

00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:49.070
Not at all.

00:22:49.070 --> 00:22:51.660
Welcome to Griffin, Gentiane!

00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:11.930
Now, then... what kind of
girls are waiting for me?

00:24:42.940 --> 00:24:45.480
Episode 2: "Wake Up."
